<div style="text-align:center; font-size:28px; font-weight:bold;">
    Writing and Appending to Files
</div>
<br>
<div style="font-size:18px;">

# Question 1: Writing a Simple Message
Create a new file named **`output/greetings.txt`** and write the message _**"Hello, World of Bioinformatics!"**_ to it.
<br></br>

# Question 2: Appending to a File
Append the message _**"Exploring file operations in Python."**_ to the file **`output/greetings.txt`** on a new line.
<br></br>

# Question 3: Writing Multiple Lines with Loop
Create a file **`output/gene_info.txt`** and use a loop to write the following genes and their functions, each on a new line: **`["BRCA1 - DNA repair", "TP53 - Cell cycle regulation", "EGFR - Signal transduction"]`**.
<br></br>

# Question 4: Using `.writelines()` to Write a List
With the list of strings **`["Sequence A: ATCG", "Sequence B: GCTA", "Sequence C: CGAT"]`**, write these to a file named **`output/sequence_list.txt`** using the **`.writelines()`** method.
<br></br>
</div>